@* ProjectPage: one project with its reviews, at "/projects/{id}". The reviews are the whole page: a progress table
   (review id with title and creation date, stage, signatures such as 2/3 with a note for out-of-date ones, blockers
   (open threads, unanswered checks, disputed checks), who a review is waiting on, last activity and due date with an
   Overdue badge), each row a link to the review. Above the table sit a summary strip (reviews per stage and overdue)
   and a filter bar (stage, overdue only, blocked only, text search); the column headers sort; 25 reviews make a page.
   All of that lives in the query string (?stage=&overdue=1&blocked=1&sort=&dir=&q=&page=), so each view has an address.
   A "+ New review" button
   that leads to the separate creation page at "/projects/{id}/reviews/new" and a "Plan reviews" button. Whoever
   may administer the project (a system administrator or a project admin) also gets a "Repositories" button to the
   repository page of the project, an "Audit trail" button to the project audit page and an "Evidence settings"
   button to the page that decides who may read the evidence anonymously and what the attestation PDFs contain, and a
   "Checklist" button to the page that imports, exports, replaces and resets the checklist new reviews start with.
   Whoever may administer the
   project also sees a Members section below the reviews: the members with a role button and a Remove button, and a
   "+ Add member" button that leads to its own page (members are rarely changed, so the form is not here and no list
   of users is ever shown). Above the members an administrator also sees a "Review rules" card with three switches
   ("Require independent reviewers", which keeps the author of a review from being its reviewer or signing it, "Authors
   cannot answer the checklist of their own review", and "The person who reopened a review cannot sign it again"; all
   three are enforced and on by default, also for projects that existed before they were enforced) and a one-line summary
   of the project's checklist (version label, size, built-in default or custom) that leads to the checklist page. A project the user may not see looks exactly like a project that does not exist.

   Presentation only; state lives in ProjectPage.razor.cs. Every interactive element and every key value carries a
   stable kebab-case data-testid (row-level ids carry the review id or the user name), and the data-interactive
   marker on the root flips to "true" once the live circuit is connected.

   Human factors: (a) the reviews, the reason for the visit, come first and the next steps are the buttons beside
   the heading; (b) the Members section is only for administrators of the project and rare member changes sit behind
   "+ Add member", so nobody else sees them; (c) an action that is not possible is replaced by a sentence that
   says why (no repository yet, no members yet, the last project admin cannot be removed).

   The page body is inside SessionGate, which replaces it with a "Session ended" message when the user is no longer
   valid while the page is open. *@
@page "/projects/{ProjectId:int}"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>@(Project?.Name ?? "Project") - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<SessionGate>
<main class="page" data-testid="project-page" data-interactive="@InteractiveMarker">
    <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/projects" data-testid="breadcrumb-projects-link">Projects</a>
        @if (Project is not null)
        {
            <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
            <span aria-current="page">@Project.Name</span>
        }
    </nav>

    @if (!Loaded)
    {
        <p class="muted" data-testid="project-loading">Loading...</p>
    }
    else if (Project is null)
    {
        <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="project-not-found">Project @ProjectId does not exist.</p>
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="page-heading">
            <h1 data-testid="project-name">@Project.Name</h1>
            <div class="heading-actions">
                @if (CanAudit)
                {
                    <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId/audit"
                       data-testid="project-audit-link">Audit trail</a>
                }
                @if (CanAdminister)
                {
                    <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId/repositories" data-testid="repositories-link">Repositories</a>
                    <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId/evidence-settings"
                       data-testid="evidence-settings-link">Evidence settings</a>
                    <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId/checklist"
                       data-testid="checklist-link">Checklist</a>
                }
                @if (CanContribute && Repositories.Count > 0)
                {
                    <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId/plan" data-testid="plan-reviews-link">Plan reviews</a>
                }
                @if (CanContribute)
                {
                    <a class="action" href="/projects/@ProjectId/reviews/new" data-testid="new-review-button">+ New review</a>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
        @if (!CanContribute)
        {
            <p class="notice" role="status" data-testid="readonly-notice">
                Your access to this project is read-only: you can read its reviews but not change them.
            </p>
        }
        @if (Project.Description.Length > 0)
        {
            <p class="page-lead" data-testid="project-description">@Project.Description</p>
        }
        @if (CanContribute && Repositories.Count == 0)
        {
            <p class="muted hint" data-testid="plan-reviews-unavailable">
                @(CanAdminister
                    ? "Planning reviews needs a repository; add one with the Repositories button."
                    : "Planning reviews needs a repository; ask a project administrator to add one.")
            </p>
        }

        <h2 class="section-title">Reviews</h2>
        @if (Progress.Count == 0)
        {
            <p class="muted" data-testid="reviews-empty">
                @(CanContribute
                    ? "This project has no reviews yet. Use + New review to add the first one."
                    : "This project has no reviews yet.")
            </p>
        }
        else
        {
            var summary = Summary;
            <p class="summary-strip" data-testid="project-summary">
                <span class="badge" data-testid="project-summary-setup">@summary.Setup in setup</span>
                <span class="badge" data-testid="project-summary-in-review">@summary.InReview in review</span>
                <span class="badge approved" data-testid="project-summary-approved">@summary.Approved approved</span>
                <span class="badge rejected" data-testid="project-summary-rejected">@summary.Rejected rejected</span>
                <span class="badge @(summary.Overdue > 0 ? "failed" : null)" data-testid="project-summary-overdue">@summary.Overdue overdue</span>
            </p>

            @* The filter bar is a plain form with a GET method, so every view has an address of its own *@
            <form class="filter-bar" method="get" action="/projects/@ProjectId" data-testid="review-filter">
                <label>Stage
                    <select name="stage" data-testid="filter-stage">
                        <option value="" selected="@(StageFilter is null)">All stages</option>
                        <option value="setup" selected="@(StageFilter == ReviewStage.Setup)">Setup</option>
                        <option value="in-review" selected="@(StageFilter == ReviewStage.InReview)">In review</option>
                        <option value="approved" selected="@(StageFilter == ReviewStage.Approved)">Approved</option>
                        <option value="rejected" selected="@(StageFilter == ReviewStage.Rejected)">Rejected</option>
                    </select>
                </label>
                <label class="switch">
                    <input type="checkbox" name="overdue" value="1" checked="@OverdueOnly" data-testid="filter-overdue" />
                    Overdue only
                </label>
                <label class="switch">
                    <input type="checkbox" name="blocked" value="1" checked="@BlockedOnly" data-testid="filter-blocked" />
                    Blocked only
                </label>
                <label>Search
                    <input type="search" name="q" value="@SearchText" maxlength="100" placeholder="Id or title"
                           data-testid="filter-search" />
                </label>
                @* Keep the sort state, also a descending order of the default column; the default (id ascending) adds nothing *@
                @if (SortColumn != "id" || Descending)
                {
                    <input type="hidden" name="sort" value="@SortColumn" />
                    <input type="hidden" name="dir" value="@(Descending ? "desc" : "asc")" />
                }
                <button type="submit" class="outline small" data-testid="filter-apply">Apply</button>
                @if (Filtered)
                {
                    <a class="action outline small" href="/projects/@ProjectId"
                       data-testid="filter-clear">Clear filters</a>
                }
            </form>

            @if (Matching.Count == 0)
            {
                <p class="muted" data-testid="reviews-no-match">No review matches the filters.</p>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="review-scroll">
                    <table class="review-table" data-testid="reviews-list">
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col" aria-sort="@AriaSort("id")"><a href="@SortAddress("id")" data-testid="sort-id">Review</a></th>
                                <th scope="col" aria-sort="@AriaSort("stage")"><a href="@SortAddress("stage")" data-testid="sort-stage">Stage</a></th>
                                <th scope="col" aria-sort="@AriaSort("signatures")"><a href="@SortAddress("signatures")" data-testid="sort-signatures">Signatures</a></th>
                                <th scope="col">Blockers</th>
                                <th scope="col">Waiting on</th>
                                <th scope="col" aria-sort="@AriaSort("activity")"><a href="@SortAddress("activity")" data-testid="sort-activity">Last activity</a></th>
                                <th scope="col" aria-sort="@AriaSort("due")"><a href="@SortAddress("due")" data-testid="sort-due">Due</a></th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            @foreach (var review in PageRows)
                            {
                                <tr class="review-row" data-testid="review-row-@review.ReviewId">
                                    <td>
                                        <a class="row-title" href="/projects/@ProjectId/reviews/@review.ReviewId" data-testid="review-link-@review.ReviewId">@review.ReviewId</a>
                                        <p class="muted" data-testid="review-title-@review.ReviewId">@review.Title</p>
                                        @if (review.FollowsReviewId is { } follows)
                                        {
                                            <p class="muted" data-testid="review-follows-@review.ReviewId">Follow-up to <a href="/projects/@ProjectId/reviews/@follows" data-testid="review-follows-link-@review.ReviewId">@follows</a></p>
                                        }
                                        <time class="muted" datetime="@review.Created.UtcDateTime.ToString("O", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)" data-testid="review-created-@review.ReviewId">@review.Created.UtcDateTime.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)</time>
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        <span class="badge @StageBadgeClass(review.Stage)" data-testid="review-approval-@review.ReviewId">@StageLabel(review.Stage)</span>
                                        @if (review.Reopened)
                                        {
                                            <span class="badge pending" data-testid="review-reopened-@review.ReviewId">Reopened</span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td>
                                        @if (review.SlotsRequired == 0)
                                        {
                                            <span class="muted" data-testid="review-progress-@review.ReviewId" title="No reviewers assigned yet">-</span>
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <span data-testid="review-progress-@review.ReviewId">@review.SlotsSigned/@review.SlotsRequired</span>
                                            @if (review.SlotsOutOfDate > 0)
                                            {
                                                <span class="muted" data-testid="review-outofdate-@review.ReviewId">@review.SlotsOutOfDate out of date</span>
                                            }
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                    <td data-testid="review-blockers-@review.ReviewId">@BlockersText(review)</td>
                                    <td data-testid="review-waiting-@review.ReviewId">@(review.WaitingOn.Count == 0 ? "-" : string.Join(", ", review.WaitingOn))</td>
                                    <td class="nowrap">
                                        <time datetime="@review.LastActivity.UtcDateTime.ToString("O", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)" data-testid="review-activity-@review.ReviewId">@review.LastActivity.UtcDateTime.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)</time>
                                    </td>
                                    <td class="nowrap">
                                        <span data-testid="review-due-@review.ReviewId">@(review.DueDate is { } due ? due.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) : "-")</span>
                                        @if (review.IsOverdue)
                                        {
                                            <span class="badge failed" data-testid="review-overdue-@review.ReviewId">Overdue</span>
                                        }
                                    </td>
                                </tr>
                            }
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>

                <p class="review-paging" data-testid="reviews-paging">
                    <span class="muted" data-testid="reviews-range">Showing @((CurrentPage - 1) * PageSize + 1)-@((CurrentPage - 1) * PageSize + PageRows.Count) of @Matching.Count</span>
                    @if (CurrentPage > 1)
                    {
                        <a href="@Address(null, false, CurrentPage - 1)" data-testid="reviews-prev">Previous</a>
                    }
                    @if (CurrentPage < PageCount)
                    {
                        <a href="@Address(null, false, CurrentPage + 1)" data-testid="reviews-next">Next</a>
                    }
                </p>
            }
        }

        @if (CanAdminister)
        {
            <h2 class="section-title">Review rules</h2>
            @if (RulesError is not null)
            {
                <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="review-rules-error">@RulesError</p>
            }
            @if (RulesStatus is not null)
            {
                <p class="notice" role="status" data-testid="review-rules-status">@RulesStatus</p>
            }
            <section class="card" data-testid="review-rules-card">
                <div class="field setting" data-testid="review-rule-independent-reviewers">
                    <label class="switch">
                        <input type="checkbox" checked="@RequireIndependentChoice"
                               @onchange="e => RequireIndependentChoice = (bool)(e.Value ?? false)"
                               data-testid="independent-reviewers-switch" />
                        Require independent reviewers
                    </label>
                    <p class="muted hint">
                        The person who created a review cannot be one of its reviewers and cannot sign it. Switch
                        this off for a project where one person has to do both. ReviewCenter only knows who created
                        the review in this tool; it does not match the authors of commits.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="field setting" data-testid="review-rule-author-checklist">
                    <label class="switch">
                        <input type="checkbox" checked="@RequireNonAuthorChoice"
                               @onchange="e => RequireNonAuthorChoice = (bool)(e.Value ?? false)"
                               data-testid="author-checklist-switch" />
                        Authors cannot answer the checklist of their own review
                    </label>
                    <p class="muted hint">
                        The person who created a review cannot answer the checks of its checklist or set which sections
                        apply; another member has to. Comment threads are not affected. Switch this off for a project
                        where one person has to do both. The rule is on by default and applies to every project,
                        including the ones created before it was enforced. Every change is recorded in the audit trail.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="field setting" data-testid="review-rule-reopener-signing">
                    <label class="switch">
                        <input type="checkbox" checked="@RequireNonReopenerChoice"
                               @onchange="e => RequireNonReopenerChoice = (bool)(e.Value ?? false)"
                               data-testid="reopener-signing-switch" />
                        The person who reopened a review cannot sign it again
                    </label>
                    <p class="muted hint">
                        The person who reopened a review cannot sign it again, and a reopen is refused when it would
                        leave a reviewer slot in which nobody may sign. Switch this off for a project where the
                        administrator who reopens a review is also its only reviewer. The rule is on by default and
                        applies to every project, including the ones created before it was enforced. Every change is
                        recorded in the audit trail.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <p>
                    <button type="button" class="outline small" data-testid="independent-reviewers-save"
                            @onclick="SaveReviewRulesAsync">Save review rules</button>
                </p>
                <div class="field setting" data-testid="review-rule-checklist">
                    <p>
                        Checklist: <span data-testid="project-checklist-summary">@ChecklistSummary</span>
                    </p>
                    <p class="muted hint">
                        The checklist that new reviews start with; existing reviews keep theirs.
                        <a href="/projects/@ProjectId/checklist" data-testid="review-rules-checklist-link">Change the checklist template</a>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <h2 class="section-title">Members</h2>
            @if (MemberError is not null)
            {
                <p class="error" role="alert" data-testid="member-error">@MemberError</p>
            }
            @if (MemberStatus is not null)
            {
                <p class="notice" role="status" data-testid="member-status">@MemberStatus</p>
            }
            @if (Members.Count == 0)
            {
                <p class="muted" data-testid="members-empty">
                    This project has no members, so only system administrators can see it. Use + Add member.
                </p>
            }
            else
            {
                <ul class="row-list" data-testid="members-list">
                    @foreach (var current in Members)
                    {
                        <li class="row-card static-row" data-testid="member-row-@current.Username">
                            <div class="row-main">
                                <strong class="row-title" data-testid="member-name-@current.Username">@current.Username</strong>
                                <p class="muted">@current.DisplayName</p>
                                <p class="row-badges">
                                    <span class="badge" data-testid="member-role-@current.Username">@RoleLabel(current.Role)</span>
                                    @if (!current.Enabled)
                                    {
                                        <span class="badge">Disabled</span>
                                    }
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="row-actions">
                                @if (current.Role == ProjectRole.Auditor)
                                {
                                    @* An auditor is never promoted by a toggle: each change names its target role *@
                                    <button type="button" class="outline small" data-testid="member-set-role-@current.Username-user"
                                            @onclick="() => SetRoleAsync(current, ProjectRole.User)">Make member</button>
                                    <button type="button" class="outline small" data-testid="member-set-role-@current.Username-projectadmin"
                                            @onclick="() => SetRoleAsync(current, ProjectRole.ProjectAdmin)">Make project admin</button>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <button type="button" class="outline small" data-testid="member-toggle-role-@current.Username"
                                            @onclick="() => ToggleRoleAsync(current)">@(current.Role == ProjectRole.ProjectAdmin ? "Make member" : "Make project admin")</button>
                                    <button type="button" class="outline small" data-testid="member-set-role-@current.Username-auditor"
                                            @onclick="() => SetRoleAsync(current, ProjectRole.Auditor)">Make auditor</button>
                                }
                                <button type="button" class="outline small" data-testid="member-remove-@current.Username"
                                        @onclick="() => RemoveMemberAsync(current)">Remove</button>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                    }
                </ul>
            }

            <p>
                <a class="action outline" href="/projects/@ProjectId/members/new"
                   data-testid="add-member-button">+ Add member</a>
            </p>
        }
    }
</main>
</SessionGate>
